Rules:
  [T1] Every public function MUST have tests.
  [T2] Test function names MUST describe what is being tested.
  [T3] Use table-driven tests for multiple cases.
  [T4] Use subtests for related assertions (`t.Run`).
  [T5] Mock external dependencies.
  [T6] Tests MUST be independent — no shared state.
  [T7] Use testify for assertions.
  [T8] Test files MUST be named `*_test.go`.

Pros:
  - Confidence in changes
  - Living documentation
  - Regression prevention

Cons:
  - Maintenance cost
  - Initial time investment

Alternatives:
  - Manual testing
  - Property-based testing

State: +

